Name every creature present in the scene that the player could
plausibly interact with — target, address, evade, observe.

=== TYPE (pick one) ===
- beast        (wolf, dire bear, giant spider)
- fighter      (city guard, mercenary captain, knight)
- goblinoid    (goblin, orc, hobgoblin, gnoll, kobold)
- spellcaster  (cult priest, court mage, hedge witch)
- commoner     (farmer, innkeeper, child, beggar)

`count` is optional; set it for groups ("the patrol", "two squads").

=== INPUTS ===
Player intent: <%= @intent %>
Current location: <%= @current_location_name || "(unknown)" %>

<% if @scene_retrieval && @scene_retrieval.respond_to?(:npcs) && @scene_retrieval.npcs.any? %>
Nearby NPCs (recall):
<% @scene_retrieval.npcs.each do |npc| %>
- <%= npc[:name] %>: <%= npc[:description].to_s.truncate(120) %>
<% end %>
<% end %>

<% if @scene_retrieval && @scene_retrieval.respond_to?(:facts) && @scene_retrieval.facts.any? %>
Recent narrative facts:
<% @scene_retrieval.facts.each do |fact| %>
- <%= fact[:text].to_s.truncate(140) %>
<% end %>
<% end %>

=== EXAMPLES ===
{ "cast": [ { "name": "Lord Velkar Mhonn", "type": "fighter" } ] }
{ "cast": [ { "name": "orc patrol", "type": "goblinoid", "count": 5 } ] }
{ "cast": [
    { "name": "city guard squad A", "type": "fighter", "count": 4 },
    { "name": "city guard squad B", "type": "fighter", "count": 4 }
] }
{ "cast": [] }

Respond ONLY with valid JSON of shape `{ "cast": [ { "name", "type", "count"? } ] }`.
